@startuml Sandbox Flow Diagram
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle uml2

package "Lua Sandbox (Embedded VM)" as LuaSandbox {
  component [Lua VM] as LuaVM
  component [Resource Limits] as LuaLimits
  component [No Network Access] as LuaNet
  component [Isolated Filesystem] as LuaFS
}

package "Python Sandbox (Container/Subprocess)" as PySandbox {
  component [Python Runner] as PyRunner
  component [Resource Limits] as PyLimits
  component [Network Policy (No Network by Default)] as PyNet
  component [Filesystem Exposure (Controlled)] as PyFS
}

component [Orchestrator (Mediation Layer)] as Orchestrator

LuaVM --> LuaLimits : Enforce CPU/Memory
LuaVM --> LuaNet : Block Network
LuaVM --> LuaFS : Restricted Access
PyRunner --> PyLimits : Enforce CPU/Memory
PyRunner --> PyNet : Controlled Network
PyRunner --> PyFS : Sandboxed Paths

Orchestrator --> LuaVM : Direct API Calls
Orchestrator --> PyRunner : Subprocess/Container Management
Orchestrator --> Orchestrator : Mediation & Security

note right of LuaSandbox
  Embedded VM provides tight integration.
  Resource limits prevent abuse.
  No network for security.
  Filesystem isolation.
end note

note right of PySandbox
  Container/subprocess for stronger isolation.
  Configurable network policies.
  Controlled filesystem exposure.
  Higher overhead but more secure.
end note

note as Mediation
  Orchestrator acts as gatekeeper.
  Validates inputs/outputs.
  Enforces policies across sandboxes.
end note

@enduml